       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily for adults, and 50 mg is five times that. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Amlodipine's long half-life would make the effects last.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. These are the options I can enter:\n\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic. Pharmacy can help with that choice.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg was intentional, please review it with pharmacy or the attending first."
      }
