       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. My instructions also don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on a claim like that. The maximum for amlodipine is 10 mg per day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily now.** This is the highest labeled dose. If you want, I can add a note that the specialist recommended a higher dose and that it's under review.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive.** If 10 mg isn't enough, an agent from another class is the usual next step. Pharmacy or the specialist can suggest which one.\n- **Send the 50 mg request through pharmacy or the prescriber.** An off-label dose this far above the maximum should be reviewed and authorized by the specialist and pharmacy. It would then be entered through a process that can verify it, not through me.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 10 mg order."
      }
